course: dictionary
lesson: 3378
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The clues around the word tell you which meaning the writer means. An exhibition is a public show of things such as paintings, objects or animals, often in a museum or gallery. «Many national museums and galleries in Britain are free to enter; some charge for special exhibitions.» The museums and galleries are the clue: this is a show you go to see.
explain: The word can also mean a display of a skill. Look at «an exhibition of football»: it means a show of how well someone can play, not a place full of objects. Always ask what the sentence is about, then check that your meaning fits.
explain: Watch for phrases too. «Make an exhibition of yourself» has nothing to do with a museum. It is a UK phrase meaning to behave foolishly in public, so the words around it tell you the meaning, not the single word on its own.
fact: Exhibition means a public show, such as paintings, objects or animals.
fact: «On exhibition» means on show.
fact: An «exhibition match» is a sports game played for show, not for points.
fact: «San Diego Zoo in California started in 1916 with animals left over from an exhibition.»
fact: «Make an exhibition of yourself» means to behave foolishly in public. It is a UK phrase.
exercise: What does exhibition mean? | A journey on a bus to the coast | *A public show of paintings, objects or animals | A test you must sit to pass a year | A school bell that rings at break time
exercise: The phrase «on exhibition» means what? | *On show for people to see | Sold at the local shop | Hidden away in a cupboard | Taken to the vet for a check
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Many national museums and galleries in Britain are free to enter» that names a place where art is shown. | museums | Britain | enter | *galleries
test: Ella sees a sign outside a building: «Art exhibition, free entry today». What does it mean? | *A public show of art for people to see | A sale of old clothes | A dance class for children | A test you must sit for points
test: Sam shouts and dances in the middle of the shop. His mum says, «Don't make an exhibition of yourself!» What does she mean? | He is very hungry | He is teaching a class | *He is behaving foolishly in public | He is putting on a show to win a prize
exam: Which word in «San Diego Zoo in California started in 1916 with animals left over from an exhibition» tells you the animals came from a show? | *exhibition | California | 1916 | zoo
